WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.251 --> 00:00:06.127
In West Africa, where I live,

00:00:06.169 --> 00:00:09.172
there are 60 million smallholder farmers.

00:00:09.214 --> 00:00:11.174
Smallholder farmers are the largest group

00:00:11.216 --> 00:00:13.510
of people living
on less than two dollars a day.

00:00:14.177 --> 00:00:17.180
Many go hungry each year
because they don't grow enough to eat.

00:00:18.139 --> 00:00:19.391
Government subsidies,

00:00:19.391 --> 00:00:23.228
which could be as much as 90 million
in a single year for a country,

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:24.729
don’t meet full demand

00:00:24.729 --> 00:00:28.400
and are often driven
to large farms and male farmers,

00:00:28.441 --> 00:00:31.319
even though women
are the backbone of farming in Africa.

00:00:32.362 --> 00:00:33.905
Despite these investments,

00:00:33.947 --> 00:00:38.285
yields per hectare haven’t increased
significantly in over four decades.

00:00:39.744 --> 00:00:44.082
So smallholder farmers earn the bulk
of their cash at harvest time,

00:00:44.082 --> 00:00:48.086
but then, fast-forward nine months later,
at planting time, they're cash-poor again.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:52.173
The prevailing assumption
is that farmers need grants,

00:00:52.215 --> 00:00:53.341
subsidies or credit

00:00:53.383 --> 00:00:55.552
in order to be able
to invest in their farms.

00:00:56.553 --> 00:00:58.805
But we found a surprising insight.

00:00:59.472 --> 00:01:03.226
The fundamental problem
isn't that farmers have no cash.

00:01:03.268 --> 00:01:05.895
It's that they don't have it
when they need it.

00:01:06.771 --> 00:01:09.232
I first came across this paradox in 2008,

00:01:09.232 --> 00:01:11.151
when I was working in microcredit.

00:01:11.943 --> 00:01:13.903
Farmers would ask me things like,

00:01:13.945 --> 00:01:16.990
“Can I over-repay my loan
for next year’s loan?”

00:01:17.324 --> 00:01:20.410
or, “Hey, could I repay my loan
a year in advance?”

00:01:21.911 --> 00:01:24.873
Even though they were using
the language of credit,

00:01:24.914 --> 00:01:28.335
what they were actually describing
was a need to save.

00:01:29.628 --> 00:01:31.963
But do farmers have any money to save?

00:01:32.922 --> 00:01:35.133
Do people living
on less than two dollars a day

00:01:35.175 --> 00:01:36.718
have any money to save?

00:01:37.677 --> 00:01:39.262
Well, it turns out that they do,

00:01:39.304 --> 00:01:41.306
just in very small increments.

00:01:41.765 --> 00:01:44.601
At a local market, they might sell
a few eggs for a dollar,

00:01:44.643 --> 00:01:46.269
or sell a goat for 10,

00:01:46.269 --> 00:01:47.812
work on someone else's farm,

00:01:47.854 --> 00:01:51.024
and over time, you can imagine
how that money could add up.

00:01:52.108 --> 00:01:54.736
But many farmers live far away from banks,

00:01:54.778 --> 00:01:57.989
so they hold that money on them,
or they hide it at home,

00:01:57.989 --> 00:02:01.576
where it's at risk
of theft, fire, even flood.

00:02:02.619 --> 00:02:05.789
And hey, even without those risks,
money at home is tempting.

00:02:05.789 --> 00:02:07.749
It's hard to hold on to cash.

00:02:08.208 --> 00:02:11.795
And sometimes, the smartest thing to do
might be to spend it.

00:02:13.588 --> 00:02:18.343
So the real problem that farmers face
is that they lack a safe place to save.

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:20.720
And if they could save,

00:02:20.762 --> 00:02:24.349
they could afford to buy what they need
to make their farms more productive

00:02:24.391 --> 00:02:26.184
and resilient to climate change.

00:02:26.559 --> 00:02:31.231
This is a 100-billion-dollar problem
in sub-Saharan Africa each year.

00:02:32.065 --> 00:02:35.735
Setou, a peanut farmer in Mali,
was facing a similar challenge.

00:02:36.486 --> 00:02:40.115
When we met in 2014,
she was feeling overwhelmed.

00:02:40.156 --> 00:02:42.492
Climate change was hurting her harvest,

00:02:42.492 --> 00:02:43.910
and at planting time,

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:47.288
she didn't even have money
to rent a cow to plow her farm,

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:50.166
let alone money
for improved seeds and fertilizer.

00:02:51.459 --> 00:02:54.713
But we realized she could have saved
for what she needed

00:02:54.754 --> 00:02:56.923
if she had a safe place to do so.

00:02:58.007 --> 00:03:02.387
Our nonprofit, myAgro, helps farmers
in Mali, Senegal and Tanzania

00:03:02.387 --> 00:03:04.431
save up, little by little,

00:03:04.472 --> 00:03:07.350
for the improved seeds
and fertilizer they need.

00:03:07.934 --> 00:03:11.104
Together, these help improve harvests

00:03:11.146 --> 00:03:13.648
and generate a 3x return
on their investment.

00:03:15.191 --> 00:03:17.402
Here's how the program works.

00:03:17.402 --> 00:03:20.405
We start with a young
entrepreneur like Demba.

00:03:20.405 --> 00:03:23.992
We equip him with a smartphone
and our app, myAgro Connect,

00:03:24.033 --> 00:03:26.828
so that he can manage his sales territory.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.873
At harvest time, Demba
visits farmers in his village

00:03:29.873 --> 00:03:32.584
and asks them if they want to sign up
for a myAgro package

00:03:32.625 --> 00:03:34.627
to improve their harvest and income.

00:03:35.628 --> 00:03:37.297
After a farmer signs up,

00:03:37.338 --> 00:03:40.049
they can pay slowly,
over the course of nine months.

00:03:41.509 --> 00:03:43.303
To collect their savings payments,

00:03:43.303 --> 00:03:47.724
we replicate the way people buy
prepaid minutes for their phone.

00:03:47.766 --> 00:03:49.017
It's really simple --

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:52.937
you buy a scratch card,
scratch off the back,

00:03:52.979 --> 00:03:54.647
and a unique code appears,

00:03:54.689 --> 00:03:56.775
which you text in
to validate your payment.

00:03:57.442 --> 00:04:02.155
We use the same technology to help farmers
save up for the planting period,

00:04:02.155 --> 00:04:04.699
and because farmers are familiar
with how it works,

00:04:04.741 --> 00:04:07.076
they trust it and use it correctly.

00:04:07.535 --> 00:04:10.371
It's also so much more transparent
than traditional methods,

00:04:10.371 --> 00:04:14.250
which is usually, you hand over your cash
to an agent, without any receipt.

00:04:15.335 --> 00:04:16.544
With our platform,

00:04:16.586 --> 00:04:18.463
we know exactly who has made a payment

00:04:18.505 --> 00:04:22.592
and when and how much the village
entrepreneur needs to transfer to us.

00:04:22.634 --> 00:04:26.012
A farmer can also pay directly
via mobile money, if they have it.

00:04:28.056 --> 00:04:31.518
Farmers are able to save up
in a way that's joyful.

00:04:31.851 --> 00:04:33.895
They often hold on to their scratch cards,

00:04:33.895 --> 00:04:36.064
and they look at them with awe and pride

00:04:36.064 --> 00:04:38.983
of how much they've been able
to save over time.

00:04:39.025 --> 00:04:42.070
It's transparent,
convenient and stress-free.

00:04:42.987 --> 00:04:45.907
Tell me, when was the last time
your bank made you that happy?

00:04:45.949 --> 00:04:47.367
(Laughter)

00:04:47.367 --> 00:04:48.743
(Applause)

00:04:48.743 --> 00:04:49.994
Designing --

00:04:49.994 --> 00:04:51.621
(Applause)

00:04:51.663 --> 00:04:56.084
Designing a savings plan this way
has made it particularly easy for women.

00:04:56.084 --> 00:05:00.129
They value the democratic access
to seeds and fertilizer,

00:05:00.129 --> 00:05:02.966
and the savings cadence matches
the small amounts of money

00:05:02.966 --> 00:05:05.134
they earn each week at local markets.

00:05:06.094 --> 00:05:09.472
In a region where 20 percent of women
own a bank account,

00:05:09.514 --> 00:05:12.100
60 percent of myAgro farmers are women.

00:05:14.018 --> 00:05:18.565
In 2021, the average myAgro farmer
grew two times more food

00:05:18.565 --> 00:05:21.317
than non-myAgro farmers in the same area.

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:25.154
This translates to 200 dollars
of additional net income.

00:05:26.531 --> 00:05:29.409
For context, for a farmer
living on 1.50 per day,

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:31.369
that's a 35 percent increase.

00:05:32.954 --> 00:05:36.624
And by expanding the purchasing power
for smallholder farmers,

00:05:36.624 --> 00:05:39.377
the financial prospects
of young entrepreneurs like Dembe

00:05:39.377 --> 00:05:40.670
are also improving.

00:05:41.546 --> 00:05:45.258
Before myAgro, he was doing OK
selling goods on his own,

00:05:45.258 --> 00:05:48.636
but now, selling seeds and fertilizer
to his community via our model,

00:05:48.678 --> 00:05:49.804
he is thriving.

00:05:50.471 --> 00:05:53.308
He bought two freezers
to expand his business,

00:05:53.308 --> 00:05:55.768
and he dreams of building
a home for his family.

00:05:56.686 --> 00:06:00.148
Last year, Dembe served
400 farmers in his village.

00:06:01.357 --> 00:06:04.444
Using a savings-led model
has many benefits.

00:06:04.485 --> 00:06:07.655
For the farmers,
it's reliable and low-stress.

00:06:07.697 --> 00:06:08.948
For the organization,

00:06:08.948 --> 00:06:12.535
it means we don't need to raise large
amounts of working capital each year.

00:06:12.577 --> 00:06:15.413
Instead, we're unlocking capital
from farmers directly.

00:06:16.956 --> 00:06:20.335
And by offering farmers
a trusted and transparent way

00:06:20.376 --> 00:06:22.462
to save their own money,

00:06:22.503 --> 00:06:25.506
they are breaking the cycle
of poverty for their families

00:06:25.548 --> 00:06:28.009
and entering a cycle
of investment and growth.

00:06:29.302 --> 00:06:30.845
Meanwhile,

00:06:30.887 --> 00:06:33.139
Setou has transformed her life,

00:06:33.181 --> 00:06:36.267
all with the power
of her own savings and farming.

00:06:37.101 --> 00:06:39.312
In 2014, she decided to try us

00:06:39.312 --> 00:06:42.065
and planted a quarter
of her peanut farm with us.

00:06:42.774 --> 00:06:44.734
Each year, with her increased profits,

00:06:44.776 --> 00:06:47.654
she reinvested a portion
in building her assets.

00:06:48.363 --> 00:06:50.823
Today, she owns ten cows,

00:06:50.865 --> 00:06:53.993
which she rents out to her neighbors
to earn additional income.

00:06:53.993 --> 00:06:58.706
(Applause)

00:06:59.123 --> 00:07:03.836
Last year, she planted her entire
one-hectare peanut farm with myAgro.

00:07:05.588 --> 00:07:06.881
And with her profit,

00:07:06.881 --> 00:07:09.842
she proudly moved her family
from their one-bedroom home ...

00:07:10.510 --> 00:07:11.678
to this.

00:07:12.553 --> 00:07:17.976
(Cheers and applause)

00:07:18.017 --> 00:07:22.605
And now, the next generation is benefiting
from Setou’s smart farm investments.

00:07:23.731 --> 00:07:26.818
When we get this model to scale,
it will be transformational.

00:07:27.485 --> 00:07:30.697
Today, we serve over 100,000 farmers,

00:07:30.697 --> 00:07:33.992
and with investments
in data and technology,

00:07:33.992 --> 00:07:36.536
our audacious vision
is to reach one million farmers

00:07:36.577 --> 00:07:38.121
in the next five years.

00:07:38.579 --> 00:07:44.002
(Cheers and applause)

00:07:44.043 --> 00:07:47.046
We believe we can harness
the power of farmers' own savings

00:07:47.088 --> 00:07:50.633
to greatly reduce poverty
and hunger in West Africa.

00:07:50.675 --> 00:07:53.219
Now is the time
to use a savings-led approach

00:07:53.261 --> 00:07:54.971
to ending poverty for farmers.

00:07:55.013 --> 00:07:56.180
Thank you.

00:07:56.222 --> 00:08:01.644
(Cheers and applause)

